content.text:
You are alone in the galley, which suits you. You've got a tin of reconstituted noodles going cold at your elbow and a ration of pepper paste you are rationing against the fortnight to come. Wits three, shadow two: you are the sort who counts the tubes. The recycler hums behind the bulkhead, which it has done wrong since Bleakhold and is clearly proud of.

No one else is registered in the crew, so you invent them to keep the table honest. Somewhere aft, the engineer is surely teaching the air scrubber to whistle, which is the only sensible explanation for the new note in the vents. The navigator, by your reckoning, is two hours into an argument with the star charts about who is lost. The cook is rumoured to exist and has never been seen with a spoon.

You stir the noodles. They do not improve.

<npc>"If anyone asks,"</npc> you tell the empty bench across from you, <npc>"the pepper paste was already gone when I got here."</npc> The recycler thumps twice, as if it has been listening.

