Vance Oduya has his own screen on the dock office wall and does not hurry. He scrolls the berth logs with one thick thumb, grunting at each cancelled mooring.

Then he stops. A tug pilot named Tamsin Reyes logged the courier's departure by hand, down to the minute, and flagged the heading as wrong for any lane. Her bunk is two decks up. Her shift ends in a quarter hour.

<npc>"She remembers everything,"</npc> Vance says. <npc>"Mostly to spite me."</npc>

